# netsurf: Navigation Timing; performance.now() counts from the page's
# start (patch 262)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 261)
#
# performance.getEntriesByType('navigation') was [], performance.timing
# had only navigationStart, and timeOrigin and now() were the engine's
# uptime. Cloudflare's challenge polls the navigation entry every 550 ms
# until the page has loaded, and polled forever.
#
#  - quickjs/macsurf_qjs.c: each realm's time origin is the start of the
#    navigation that made it (the browser window's last_action, read in
#    js_newthread), as a browser's is; __macsurf_monotonic_ms()
#    (performance.now(), animation-frame timestamps) and native events'
#    timeStamp count from it. So responseStart includes the network's wait:
#    the Guardian reads it to decide whether the page is "performing
#    poorly" (with no entry at all it always was).
#  - vita_polyfill.js: performance.timeOrigin is that moment on the epoch
#    clock; one PerformanceNavigationTiming entry (getEntries,
#    getEntriesByType, getEntriesByName) and performance.timing over it
#    record the moments the page reaches -- its response (the realm is made
#    when the document starts to parse), interactive, DOMContentLoaded,
#    complete, load. Network phases the engine does not measure read 0.
#
# Gate: JS-frame-realm.html checks 8-11.
